 # Cyber Threat Brief — 2026-10-05

16 articles reviewed from the last 24 hours.
## Top things to know today

* *Citrix NetScaler* zero-day (CVE-2026-88779) is under active exploitation and can knock SAML deployments offline; some hits landed on appliances patched only days earlier.
* Denmark's national population register was breached, exposing data on roughly *8.8 million people*.

## Threat Actor TTPs & Campaigns

* Attackers are actively exploiting a memory overflow zero-day in *Citrix NetScaler* ADC/Gateway (CVE-2026-88779, CVSS 8.7) that can take down SAML-based deployments; researchers are also probing it for potential RCE. Source: [The Hacker News](https://thehackernews.com/2026/10/new-netscaler-zero-day-exploited-in.html)
* Attackers are targeting a critical *Rejetto HFS* flaw (CVE-2026-61500) rooted in a weak PRNG, allowing predictable session-signing keys that enable admin session forgery and remote code execution. Source: [The Hacker News](https://thehackernews.com/2026/10/attackers-target-rejetto-hfs-flaw-that.html)

## Breaches & Incidents

* Denmark is investigating a breach of its national population register after unauthorized access exposed data on about *8.8 million people*. Source: [The Record](https://therecord.media/denmark-breach-register-cyberattack)

